 Experiment 49: To Test Login Functionality of a Student Portal Where Hundreds of Students Login Simultaneously and Analyze Server Stability

AIM
To test the login functionality of a student portal by simulating hundreds of students logging in simultaneously using Apache JMeter and analyze server stability.

ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter.
2. Create a new Test Plan.
3. Add a Thread Group to simulate multiple students.
4. Set the number of users to 500.
5. Set the ramp-up period and loop count.
6. Add an HTTP Request Sampler.
7. Enter the student portal login URL.
8. Select the POST method.
9. Enter valid student login credentials as request parameters.
10. Add HTTP Header Manager and Response Assertion.
11. Run the test and collect server response details.
12. Analyze response time, throughput, error rate, and server stability.

## CONFIGURATION

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| Testing Tool | Apache JMeter |
| Application | Student Portal |
| Request Method | POST |
| Number of Users | 500 |
| Ramp-up Period | 100 seconds |
| Loop Count | 1 |
| Test Type | Load Testing |

## INPUT

**Sample login request:**

```text
URL: https://example.com/student/login
Method: POST

Username: student001
Password: Test@123
```

**Expected successful response:**

```json
{
  "status": "success",
  "message": "Login successful"
}
```

## OUTPUT

The following metrics are analyzed using Apache JMeter:

| Metric | Description |
|---|---|
| Average Response Time | Average time taken to process login requests |
| Throughput | Number of login requests processed per second |
| Error Rate | Percentage of failed login requests |
| Minimum Response Time | Lowest response time |
| Maximum Response Time | Highest response time |
| Server Stability | Ability to handle simultaneous login requests |

**Expected output format:**

```text
Student Portal Login Load Test

Total Simulated Users: 500
Ramp-up Period: 100 seconds

Login Requests: Completed
Average Response Time: Recorded by JMeter
Throughput: Recorded by JMeter
Error Rate: Recorded by JMeter

Server Stability: Analyzed
Load Testing Completed.
```

## RESULT
Thus, the student portal login functionality was tested using Apache JMeter by simulating 500 concurrent students. Server stability was analyzed using response time, throughput, and error rate.
